.TH MATLOCK 1 "10 July 2026" "tvsos" "TVSOS Commands Manual"

\"------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SH NAME

.B matlock
\- screen lock for X and Wayland with raining characters like in the film
\fIThe Matrix\fP (1999).

\"------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SH SYNOPSIS

.SY
.nf
\fBmatlock\fR [\-v] [<command> [<args...>]]
.fi
.YS

\"------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
\fBmatlock\fP, or Matrix Lock, is a screen lock program for X and Wayland
written in C++. Initially a fork of the original C implementation
\fBslock\fP, it has undergone considerable restructuring and revamping.

If provided, [<command> [<args...>]] is executed after the screen has been
unlocked.

.SS BACKENDS
.PP
The display backend is chosen at runtime: if \fIWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fP is set,
\fBmatlock\fP locks the session through the Wayland
\fIext-session-lock-v1\fP protocol; otherwise, if \fIDISPLAY\fP is set, the
X11 backend is used. An error is printed when neither is set.

On Wayland, the compositor must support \fIext-session-lock-v1\fP. This
includes niri, sway, river, Hyprland, KWin and other wlroots-based
compositors; GNOME (Mutter) does not implement the protocol and is not
supported. Every output is covered by a lock surface, including outputs
plugged in while the session is locked.

.SS SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.PP
On X11, to make sure a locked screen can not be bypassed by switching VTs or
killing the X server with Ctrl+Alt+Backspace, it is recommended to disable
them both in \fBxorg.conf(5)\fP for maximum security:

.EX
Section "ServerFlags"
    Option "DontVTSwitch" "True"
    Option "DontZap"      "True"
EndSection
.EE

On Wayland, input exclusivity and the hiding of screen content are
guaranteed by the compositor as part of the session-lock protocol; no
further configuration is needed.

.SS CUSTOMISATION
.PP
\fBmatlock\fP reads \fI/etc/matlock.yaml\fP and then per-user overrides from
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/matlock/matlock.yaml\fP (usually
\fI~/.config/matlock/matlock.yaml\fP). Both files are watched while the
screen is locked and changes apply live. Only a flat "key: value" YAML
subset is supported.

.TP
.B background
background colour ("#RRGGBB").
.TP
.B font_pattern
\fBfontconfig\fP(1) pattern for the rain glyphs (Wayland backend only; the
X11 backend uses core bitmap fonts).
.TP
.B font_size
pixel size of the closest rain layer (10..128). The farthest layer is fixed
at 10 and the layers between interpolate linearly.
.TP
.B mutate_chars
whether characters in the falling columns mutate (true/false).
.TP
.B failonclear
treat cleared input as a failed attempt (true/false).
.TP
.B fontcolour
mapping with \fBinit\fP, \fBinput\fP and \fBfailed\fP colours ("#RRGGBB")
for the three states.

.PP
The user and group privileges are dropped to remain compile-time settings in
\fIinclude/config.hpp\fP.

\"------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SH OPTIONS

.IP "\-v"
print version information to the standard output and exit.

\"------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SH FILES

.TP
.I /etc/matlock.yaml
system-wide configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/matlock/matlock.yaml
per-user overrides (usually \fI~/.config/matlock/matlock.yaml\fP).

